{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Energy shield impact",
  "description": "A shot stops against a personal energy shield. On the hit, a spitting 'tzzsh' of discharge where the round is vaporised, and the field itself is struck: it behaves like a huge thin glass bowl, but a dented one whose ring is chopped by a square-wave ring modulator and overdriven, so instead of a bell it gives a snarling, beating electric clang that soon dies away. The surface crackles outward from the hit as the charge spreads. Under it a low unstable buzz dips and recovers: the field bowing in and springing back.",
